---
description: Drafting and rewriting technical paper prose
globs: papers/**/*.{md,tex,txt}
alwaysApply: false
---

When drafting or revising manuscript text:

- Lead each section with its job (motivation, method, evidence, positioning).
- Prefer precise verbs and measurable claims over hype.
- Keep paragraphs short; one idea per paragraph.
- For methods: define inputs, outputs, assumptions, and complexity where relevant.
- For experiments: state setup before results; separate observation from interpretation.
- Mark uncertain content with TODO comments instead of inventing details.
- Preserve LaTeX/Markdown structure and labels already in the file.
- Suggest title/abstract last unless asked earlier — they should reflect the final contribution.
